  📋 SIGNAL (all required — evaluated on the most recent 2 weekly
  candles per ticker; a slow, weekly-timeframe pattern, not a
  rolling daily-window scan)

  1) PREVIOUS WEEK RED: closed below its open.
  2) CURRENT WEEK GREEN: closes above its open.
  3) REVERSAL MAGNITUDE: current week's % gain exceeds
     reversal_multiplier (2x) the previous week's
     % decline — e.g. a -5% week followed by a +10%+ week.
  4) STRUCTURE: current week's close is above the WEEKLY 50-period
     SMA (a moving average of weekly closes, ~1 year of history —
     not the usual daily SMA50).

  📋 DATA SOURCING
  Only 1 download per ticker: daily bars (~700 days, ~7 years —
  needed to build 50+ weekly bars for a stable weekly SMA50),
  resampled to weekly ('W') — no separate network calls needed.

  📋 OUTPUT (reasonable defaults — not explicitly requested)
  Entry_Price = the current week's CLOSE
  Stop_Loss   = the previous week's LOW
  Curr_Week / Prev_Week = the two weekly periods compared (YYYY-MM-DD)

  📋 SCORE (0-100)
  Reversal size beyond 2x (0-35) + current week's gain
  magnitude (0-25) + distance price sits above the weekly SMA50
  (0-20) + base points for clearing every gate (20)

